{"findings":[{"rule_id":"MF-005","evidence":[{"kind":"title_block","ref":"heat_treatment","page":1,"quote":"---"},{"kind":"note","ref":"N1","page":1,"quote":"HEAT TREATMENT NOTE:- 1) TO BE TOUGHENED UPTO 24-32 HRC. 2) THREADS TO BE KEEP SOFT. 3) RETAPPING TO BE DONE AFTER SURFACE TREATMENT AT SUPPLIER END.( IF APPLICABLE )"},{"kind":"note","ref":"N3","page":1,"quote":"NOTE:- 1)TO BE TOUGHENED TO 28-30 HRc."}],"comment":"The title block heat treatment field is '---' while notes N1 and N3 both call out toughening to a hardness range, so the required heat treatment is not captured in the designated field. Additionally, N1 specifies 24-32 HRC and N3 specifies 28-30 HRc, giving two conflicting hardness ranges with no indication of which applies where. The designer should fill the heat treatment field and reconcile or clarify the two hardness requirements so the shop knows exactly what to apply and where."
  ,
  "recommended_correction":"Enter the heat treatment specification in the title block and resolve the conflict between N1 (24-32 HRC) and N3 (28-30 HRc), clarifying which requirement governs or which features each applies to."}]}
